{"id": "EUVD-2026-86773", "enisaUuid": "3f3b88f1-f154-36e0-b93b-123c8210f660", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Take the reference before publishing the named histogram trigger\n\nevent_hist_trigger_named_init() puts the trigger on the global\nnamed_triggers list and only then takes the reference on the trigger it\nshares its histogram with:\n\n\tdata->ref++;\n\n\tsave_named_trigger(data->named_data->name, data);\n\n\tret = event_hist_trigger_init(data->named_data);\n\tif (ret < 0) {\n\t\tkfree(data->cmd_ops);\n\t\tdata->cmd_ops = &trigger_hist_cmd;\n\t}\n\n\treturn ret;\n\nevent_hist_trigger_init() fails when alloc_hist_pad() cannot allocate, and\nnothing takes the trigger back off the list on the way out.\nevent_hist_trigger_parse() frees it, and the next lookup by name reads the\nfreed object:\n\n BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in find_named_trigger+0xac/0xc0\n Read of size 8 at addr ffff888009346860 by task init/1\n  find_named_trigger+0xac/0xc0\n  hist_register_trigger+0xc1/0xa00\n  event_hist_trigger_parse+0x3146/0x6af0\n  event_trigger_write+0xce/0x160\n Freed by task 67:\n  kfree+0x154/0x420\n  trigger_kthread_fn+0xfd/0x160\n\nDo the reference first and publish once it has succeeded, so that nothing\nwhich can fail runs after the trigger becomes findable.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e5c5dad169fb569161d3eed6c3f6a59e65db1830", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6fb2f5370a9a6aec325ab2db1ca3d1a881499b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ffaade3611bd9501bc0b9d5d19fc75bfee7a16b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91c15cdda6033e2439f5975b938754152f3d6e38", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fe23b8eaba0d3372c66b7b31204408da0715edc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97919", "GHSA-6vf7-pxhp-xpjv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "109579a9-1712-3a9c-b19c-7949070c1b1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e53a8dcd36b9ebc9229450eb594ae20e0b2ae0fd <b6fb2f5370a9a6aec325ab2db1ca3d1a881499b8"}, {"id": "19d724d6-a2c9-361d-9190-79b891ed2a1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "740dab2338f70d93aa8235db5a9541d846d7b21c"}, {"id": "26b49f05-eeef-318a-8a23-45d96c5ff339", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7ab0fc61ce73040f89b12d76a8279995ec283541 <0fe23b8eaba0d3372c66b7b31204408da0715edc"}, {"id": "3f6eb8df-a0ae-3baf-a552-7c9171208e47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7ab0fc61ce73040f89b12d76a8279995ec283541 <2ffaade3611bd9501bc0b9d5d19fc75bfee7a16b"}, {"id": "4297e7ac-d5bd-3ac0-b015-4f5d24c65a50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15.3 <6.16"}, {"id": "6201dcf5-f98d-34f1-800c-ce5d2ae02b9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.34 <6.12.112"}, {"id": "642047a5-9fb2-32c2-9c2b-1f1fde6d2a2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7ab0fc61ce73040f89b12d76a8279995ec283541 <91c15cdda6033e2439f5975b938754152f3d6e38"}, {"id": "65dcfbe0-68c7-3a0b-bc9d-650587c619c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "74d2adc0-ed25-3dbc-adce-057a36af5eba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "74dfb3d7-5400-3e75-bc3e-7cd72ca8d503", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ac7ab38c271ba2edaeb0dc35b200ec13339776ae <e5c5dad169fb569161d3eed6c3f6a59e65db1830"}, {"id": "887a4368-fbc2-3af7-8dfe-4cfb05d0c296", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "a8667f17-9103-3063-aa8a-9738f424992e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produ